==Scots==

===Etymology===
From Middle English '''h(o)us''' < Old English '''[[hus|hūs]]''' (dwelling, shelter, house) < {{proto|Germanic|khusan|lang=sco}}, of unknown origin.

===Pronunciation===
* hUs, /hUs/

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An abode of a human being, a place that a human built to live in; a [[house]].

